  "analysis": "• **Prévia Assurances (d1, d2, d3) | 3 docs, 1 704 €**\n  - *Ambiguity:* d1 (“Prélèvement sur le compte FR76…”) debited from SELARL but is personal PER; d2 (“Assuré : M. Paul Morel”) is spouse’s life insurance; d3 (“Souscripteur : SELARL”) covers Hélène personally. *Fact needed:* Contract ownership vs payment source.\n  - *Question:* Are these Prévia contracts business (SELARL), personal (Hélène/Paul), or LMNP?\n  - *Answers/Rules:* “All business” → always selarl-morel; “All personal” → always paul/helene; “Mixed” → depends on insured person/subscriber; ask each time.\n\n• **Atelier Bois & Co (d5, d6) | 2 docs, 6 250 €**\n  - *Ambiguity:* d5 (“Chantier : 4 rue du Port”) matches LMNP; d6 (“Meuble de rangement salle de stérilisation”) matches practice, but addressee is personal. *Fact needed:* Work location/beneficiary.\n  - *Question:* Do these works belong to the LMNP flat or the SELARL practice?\n  - *Answers/Rules:* “LMNP” → always lmnp-port; “SELARL” → always selarl-morel; “Split/Personal” → depends on site address; ask each time.\n\n• **Banque Rivage & Orélia (d4, d7) | 2 docs, ~730 €**\n  - *Ambiguity:* d4 (“LOYER 4 RUE DU PORT”) shows a joint account funding the LMNP; d7 (“ligne installée au 4 rue du Port”) is an ISP at the flat billed to Paul. *Fact needed:* Account/bill purpose.\n  - *Question:* Are the Rivage account and Orélia bill personal or LMNP business?\n  - *Answers/Rules:* “LMNP” → always lmnp-port; “Personal” → always paul/helene; “Mixed” → depends on account holder/site; ask each time.",
